# Code owners — who is asked to review a change. Requests are automatic for pull requests;
# whether an approval from an owner is *required* is a branch-protection setting, not this file.
#
# CredMgr currently has a single code owner, so one rule covers the repository. The paths below
# are listed anyway so that, if a second owner is added, the security-critical surfaces are
# already marked and can be reassigned without a search.

*                                   @Cryptosours

# The vault itself: key hierarchy, envelope format, access decisions, the broker and its wire protocol.
/v2/crates/                         @Cryptosours
/v1/lib/                            @Cryptosours

# CI, release and supply-chain policy: a change here changes what "green" means.
/.github/                           @Cryptosours
/v2/deny.toml                       @Cryptosours
/v2/scripts/release.sh              @Cryptosours

# Security and licence documents.
/SECURITY.md                        @Cryptosours
/LICENSE                            @Cryptosours
/v2/DONATE.md                       @Cryptosours
/v1/DONATE.md                       @Cryptosours
